Leantime on FenrirOS
====================

Code in /usr/share/leantime (web root: public/). Its config/ directory is
/etc/leantime (the samples are there); uploaded files, storage/ (logs,
sessions, caches), bootstrap/cache and database backups live in
/var/lib/leantime. PHP runs as _php.

1. Create a MariaDB database and user for Leantime:
     CREATE DATABASE leantime CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
     CREATE USER 'leantime'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<password>';
     GRANT ALL ON leantime.* TO 'leantime'@'localhost';
2. cp /etc/leantime/sample.env /etc/leantime/.env, chgrp _php it (mode
   0640) and set LEAN_APP_URL, the LEAN_DB_* settings and, importantly,
   LEAN_SESSION_PASSWORD (the sample's value is public; use e.g.
   `openssl rand -hex 32`). The sample has LEAN_ALLOW_TELEMETRY = true
   (a daily anonymous summary to telemetry.leantime.io); set it to false
   to turn that off. Logs: LEAN_LOG_PATH='/var/lib/leantime/storage/logs/leantime.log'.
3. nginx: /usr/share/doc/leantime/nginx-leantime.conf (and, optionally, the
   php-fpm pool php-fpm-leantime.conf); enable php-fpm and nginx
   (dinitctl enable php-fpm nginx), then open https://<host>/install and
   create the first account.
4. Scheduler: cp /usr/share/doc/leantime/leantime.cron /etc/cron.d/leantime
   and dinitctl enable crond.
